  "description": "The power history is not a table: it is generated by six-group point kinetics from a $3 reactivity insertion (a step), a 40 us prompt generation time and a prompt fuel-temperature coefficient of -1e-4 dk/k/K, for 100 pins of 0.5 m with the modelled slice at the average power, starting from 1 kW of reactor power. The feedback temperature is the fuel's own average if the heat stayed where it was made, using the fuel's heat capacity (3 MJ/m3/K); the results check it against the pin's real average. The delayed-neutron data are Keepin's U-235 set; the other numbers are chosen, not any reactor's. Thermal only for the pin; no control action, coolant or void feedback.",
